==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ru|со-}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*sъ-|*sъ(n)-}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*ḱom}}. See {{cog|sla-pro|*sъ(n)}} for more information. The {{IPAchar|/n/}} persists in {{m|ru|снять}} (originally a prefixed derivative of {{m|ru|ять||to [[take]]}}), from which other words in {{m|ru|-нять}} were produced by {{glossary|reanalysis}}. See also {{m|ru|с}}, {{cog|orv|съ}}, and compare the analogous loss of ''-n-'' in {{m|ru|в-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|с-}} {{i|before vowels and all consonants except those noted below}}
* {{ru-IPA|з-}} {{i|before voiced obstruents except for {{lang|ru|в}} and {{lang|ru|ж}}}}
* {{ru-IPA|ж-}} {{i|before {{lang|ru|ж}}, where it forms a long consonant {{IPAchar|/ʐː/}}, as in e.g. {{m|ru|сжечь}}}}
* {{ru-IPA|ш-}} {{i|before {{lang|ru|ш}}, where it forms a long consonant {{IPAchar|/ʂː/}}, as in e.g. {{m|ru|сшить}}}}
* {{ru-IPA-manual|[ɕ]}} {{i|before {{lang|ru|ч}}, as in e.g. {{m|ru|счита́ть}}}}

===Prefix===
{{head|ru|prefix|cat2=verbal prefixes}}

# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} {{gloss|describing an action moving from a single position or many positions into another single position}}
#:* {{prefixusex|ru|лить|pos1=imperfective|t1=to pour|слить|pos2=perfective|t2=to pour into one place}}
# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[down]] {{gloss|describing a downward action}}
#:* {{prefixusex|ru|ходи́ть|pos1=imperfective|t1=to go|сходи́ть|pos2=perfective|t2=to go down}}
# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[off]], from [[off]] {{gloss|describing an action of removing oneself to another location}}

